WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
If you encounter a large or deep wound where blood is flowing or spurting continuously

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.440
and does not stop with basic pressure, it is a much more serious situation.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.200
Major External Bleeding It's defined as severe bleeding from a large

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:20.200
or deep wound where blood is flowing or spurting continuously and simply does not stop with

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.620
basic pressure.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.040
This is a life-threatening emergency.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:29.980
Your very first step is to call 911 immediately, then have the person sit or lie down and apply

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.259
direct firm pressure using gauze or a clean cloth.

00:00:34.259 --> 00:00:39.259
If the gauze ever becomes saturated with blood, do not remove that bottom layer.

00:00:39.259 --> 00:00:43.500
Just keep adding more gauze on top and maintain that constant pressure.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.400
If your first aid kit has hemostatic dressings available, use them.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.939
They contain a special chemical that helps blood clot much faster.

00:00:50.939 --> 00:00:55.419
After the bleeding stops, you can use a pressure bandage to hold all that gauze in place while

00:00:55.419 --> 00:00:56.660
you wait for help.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:01.660
However, if the bleeding just won't stop and EMS has not arrived yet, you may need

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.540
to start packing the wound.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:08.660
This involves taking a stack of gauze, pressing it deep into the wound itself, and applying

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.820
direct pressure on top of that.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.660
Let's practice wrapping a wound and holding pressure with a partner.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:19.019
I want you to place the gauze squares on one of your partner's limbs, then use the gauze

00:01:19.019 --> 00:01:22.820
roll we passed out earlier to wrap around the gauze squares.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.900
Your instructor will demonstrate the wrapping technique first, and then you and your partner

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:31.580
can practice together to make sure that wrap is secure and applying steady pressure.

